1
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:45,599
Commissar Tan.

2
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:46,480
You're back.

3
00:01:47,959 --> 00:01:48,439
Easy now, easy.

4
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:51,760
You had a few drinks, right?

5
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:53,480
I did.

6
00:01:53,879 --> 00:01:55,079
You signed out to go relax,

7
00:01:55,079 --> 00:01:56,519
but went all by yourself without inviting me.

8
00:01:57,519 --> 00:01:59,920
I accomplished something big today.

9
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:01,159
I'm happy.

10
00:02:01,439 --> 00:02:02,560
So I had a few drinks by myself.

11
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:05,439
What is it

12
00:02:05,799 --> 00:02:06,760
that made you this happy?

13
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:10,680
What is it?

14
00:02:34,319 --> 00:02:35,560
That piece of land by the sea...

15
00:02:37,919 --> 00:02:38,400
I rented it.

16
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:42,400
The village asked for 180,000.

17
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:48,439
I talked them down to 90,000.

18
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:59,719
You wanted to rent that place

19
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:01,840
to build a training ground, right?

20
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:09,759
Was it a good deal or what?

21
00:03:12,199 --> 00:03:13,319
Take me with you next time.

22
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:21,719
Totally worth it.

23
00:03:25,759 --> 00:03:26,840
I did the math carefully.

24
00:03:28,439 --> 00:03:29,719
With another 120,000,

25
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:34,639
we can build a temporary training ground

26
00:03:36,159 --> 00:03:37,360
to prepare for the Combat Skills Competition.

27
00:03:47,159 --> 00:03:48,560
What about the rest of the money?

28
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:54,240
I'll figure something out.

29
00:03:59,639 --> 00:04:01,599
That's not a small amount.

30
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,120
We'll figure it out together.

31
00:04:06,639 --> 00:04:07,280
What money?

32
00:04:10,319 --> 00:04:11,159
Are we getting bonuses again?

33
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:29,959
Come in.

34
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:31,560
Chief Guo, are we interrupting?

35
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:33,439
You are.

36
00:04:36,079 --> 00:04:38,199
It's never good news when you two show up.

37
00:04:38,839 --> 00:04:39,160
Have a seat.

38
00:04:50,079 --> 00:04:50,560
What's up?

39
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:55,519
Got a new idea again?

40
00:04:57,399 --> 00:04:58,319
Want another First-Class Merit?

41
00:04:58,680 --> 00:04:59,519
No, no, no.

42
00:05:00,199 --> 00:05:01,839
Of course not. Not at all.

43
00:05:02,439 --> 00:05:03,639
Honors on the wall

44
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:06,120
aren't as good as a solid foundation.

45
00:05:06,279 --> 00:05:08,160
All right, stop beating around the bush.

46
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:09,040
Liao Bufan, tell me.

47
00:05:10,439 --> 00:05:10,839
What is it?

48
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:15,040
To prep for the Combat Skills Competition,

49
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:17,040
we need funding.

50
00:05:19,879 --> 00:05:21,959
See? It's not about a First-Class Merit.

51
00:05:25,319 --> 00:05:26,360
You're taking a jab at me.

52
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,120
You don't want medals, you want funding.

53
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,360
Actually, about the training ground...

54
00:05:35,360 --> 00:05:36,360
If it could be approved,

55
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:38,120
I would've sorted it out for you long ago.

56
00:05:39,439 --> 00:05:41,839
We have a solution now.

57
00:05:42,439 --> 00:05:43,439
Would you like to hear it?

58
00:05:46,439 --> 00:05:47,240
Let's hear it.

59
00:05:48,399 --> 00:05:50,240
We found an empty lot by the sea.

60
00:05:50,680 --> 00:05:51,959
We've talked it out with the villagers.

61
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:54,560
We're thinking of putting it to use

62
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:57,240
and building a temporary training ground.

63
00:05:59,040 --> 00:05:59,839
A classmate of mine

64
00:05:59,959 --> 00:06:01,079
has a factory on Jixian Road.

65
00:06:01,639 --> 00:06:02,680
The equipment in there,

66
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:04,279
the cutting and welding tools,

67
00:06:04,319 --> 00:06:05,079
he'll let me use them all.

68
00:06:05,439 --> 00:06:07,639
As for the equipment

69
00:06:07,639 --> 00:06:08,560
for this temporary ground,

70
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:10,120
we can weld it ourselves.

71
00:06:10,439 --> 00:06:11,720
Isn't that a great idea?

72
00:06:12,279 --> 00:06:14,680
So it's not about money at all, right?

73
00:06:15,199 --> 00:06:16,639
It is about money, too.

74
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:18,680
We've budgeted carefully,

75
00:06:19,319 --> 00:06:21,560
and we need 210,000.

76
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:29,800
You need 210,000 for a temporary one?

77
00:06:30,879 --> 00:06:32,079
We've saved wherever we could.

78
00:06:44,519 --> 00:06:46,519
I can only approve 100,000.

79
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,040
That's enough.

80
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:49,040
That's enough.

81
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:49,560
That's enough.

82
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:54,199
Do you really have that much wiggle room?

83
00:06:54,279 --> 00:06:54,959
No, Chief Guo.

84
00:06:55,959 --> 00:06:57,959
We started a crowdfunding campaign

85
00:06:58,199 --> 00:06:59,120
within the Special Police Unit.

86
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:01,800
Commissar Tan gave three months' salary.

87
00:07:01,959 --> 00:07:03,120
Didn't you give three months' salary too?

88
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:04,480
Everyone chipped in and raised 87,000.

89
00:07:04,519 --> 00:07:05,560
All the team members did their best.

90
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:20,079
That's still not enough.

91
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:22,240
We'll figure something out for the rest.

92
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:24,240
There has to be a way.

93
00:07:30,279 --> 00:07:30,879
Count me in.

94
00:09:46,679 --> 00:09:48,080
Move it! Move it!

95
00:10:03,559 --> 00:10:04,000
Reporting, sir.

96
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:07,000
Wang Yunsheng requests to rejoin the team.

97
00:10:08,639 --> 00:10:10,720
Wang Yunsheng, what's all this about?

98
00:10:11,679 --> 00:10:12,440
I'm just requesting to return.

99
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:17,000
Is the Special Police Unit a place

100
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:18,360
you can come and go as you please?

101
00:10:19,919 --> 00:10:20,480
Commissar Tan,

102
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:22,720
after you criticized me last time,

103
00:10:23,279 --> 00:10:24,679
I've been reflecting on it.

104
00:10:25,519 --> 00:10:27,000
I was blinded by the desire for merit

105
00:10:27,879 --> 00:10:29,559
and ignored my duty as a police officer.

106
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:31,480
I almost lost myself.

107
00:10:33,039 --> 00:10:35,039
Being in the Special Police is my dream.

108
00:10:36,799 --> 00:10:38,000
I want to return to where I belong.

109
00:10:41,919 --> 00:10:43,120
You're already twenty-nine.

110
00:10:44,279 --> 00:10:45,679
If you don't get commended soon,

111
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:48,000
you'll never become a regular officer.

112
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:51,000
Go back.

113
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:53,559
Reporting to Chief Liao,

114
00:10:53,919 --> 00:10:54,639
I can't go back.

115
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:56,840
Director Ji already approved my transfer.

116
00:10:56,919 --> 00:10:58,000
If you don't agree,

117
00:10:58,120 --> 00:10:59,159
I'll have to turn in my uniform.

118
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:00,919
Who are you threatening?

119
00:11:02,799 --> 00:11:03,440
Reporting, sir.

120
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:06,240
I'm willing to serve as auxiliary police

121
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:07,919
and stay in the Special Police Unit.

122
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:27,279
His heart is back.

123
00:11:31,759 --> 00:11:33,240
Wang Yunsheng, fall in.

124
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:37,799
Falling in.

125
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:40,399
He's back.

126
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:23,320
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

127
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:45,679
I really need to lose this gut.

128
00:12:46,279 --> 00:12:47,320
It's getting out of hand.

129
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:49,200
It ruins the Special Police Unit's image.

130
00:12:49,759 --> 00:12:50,559
Train with us.

131
00:12:52,639 --> 00:12:53,080
Train with us.

132
00:13:17,279 --> 00:13:18,440
Keep going, keep going! Faster, faster!

133
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:18,879
Faster!

134
00:13:23,919 --> 00:13:24,879
It's faster on the way down!

135
00:13:35,879 --> 00:13:36,559
Again!

136
00:13:36,919 --> 00:13:37,279
Again!

137
00:13:38,039 --> 00:13:38,720
Pick up the pace!

138
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:03,120
Commissar Tan, are you okay?

139
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:04,279
Don't look at me. Don't look at me.

140
00:14:04,279 --> 00:14:05,159
Keep going. Keep going. Keep going.

141
00:15:15,879 --> 00:15:18,159
Come on, Commissar Tan! You got this!

142
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:54,720
Hurry, hurry! Keep the rhythm!

143
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:56,480
Coach.

144
00:17:59,799 --> 00:18:00,720
Don't move. Don't move!

145
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:03,160
Wait, how did I fall?

146
00:18:03,559 --> 00:18:04,000
What happened?

147
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:04,319
Can you get up?

148
00:18:04,359 --> 00:18:05,359
Here, help me up. Help me up.

149
00:18:06,119 --> 00:18:06,599
Slowly.

150
00:18:08,599 --> 00:18:09,079
What's wrong?

151
00:18:09,079 --> 00:18:09,400
What's going on?

152
00:18:09,839 --> 00:18:11,400
I can't feel my legs.

153
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:13,480
My legs are... they're numb.

154
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:16,559
The nucleus pulposus broke through the

155
00:18:17,359 --> 00:18:18,839
annulus fibrosus into the spinal canal.

156
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:21,960
It's not just a lumbar disc herniation.

157
00:18:22,480 --> 00:18:23,240
This is a prolapse.

158
00:18:24,240 --> 00:18:25,160
If you keep dragging this out,

159
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:26,240
do you know what'll happen?

160
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:28,640
I don't.

161
00:18:29,039 --> 00:18:30,039
What did I tell you last year?

162
00:18:32,119 --> 00:18:33,559
You told me last year

163
00:18:34,359 --> 00:18:36,599
to come see you for treatment sooner,

164
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:38,640
and not to do strenuous exercise.

165
00:18:39,319 --> 00:18:39,839
What about the year before?

166
00:18:41,079 --> 00:18:42,319
Wasn't it the same old thing?

167
00:18:43,079 --> 00:18:45,160
Why don't you leaders do something?

168
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:47,039
He should've rested a long time ago.

169
00:18:47,720 --> 00:18:48,400
Let alone training,

170
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:50,440
he should be careful just moving around.

171
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:54,079
Um...

172
00:18:55,279 --> 00:18:55,720
Director Li.

173
00:18:56,599 --> 00:18:57,359
Let me ask you for a favor.

174
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:01,319
After the Combat Skills Competition?

175
00:19:01,519 --> 00:19:02,599
You need surgery immediately.

176
00:19:03,119 --> 00:19:03,920
If you keep doing this,

177
00:19:04,559 --> 00:19:05,519
you'll be paralyzed.

178
00:19:06,319 --> 00:19:07,200
It won't be that bad, right?

179
00:19:07,759 --> 00:19:09,279
You can still recover after the surgery,

180
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,000
but don't push yourself anymore.

181
00:19:11,720 --> 00:19:12,160
Take good care of yourself.

182
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:14,119
No, no, no.

183
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:15,400
Um, later on...

184
00:19:15,759 --> 00:19:17,480
give me a Nerve block before I go on.

185
00:19:17,480 --> 00:19:18,160
Would that work?

186
00:19:20,640 --> 00:19:22,200
What do you mean don't push myself?

187
00:19:26,839 --> 00:19:28,839
You've had this condition for years.

188
00:19:31,680 --> 00:19:32,960
It's been a few years, hasn't it?

189
00:19:33,279 --> 00:19:35,319
It just started as a lumbar muscle strain.

190
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:36,839
Who doesn't have a lumbar muscle strain?

191
00:19:37,440 --> 00:19:38,759
You just bear with it and it passes.

192
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:42,039
You joined traffic police because of this.

193
00:19:45,599 --> 00:19:48,400
Weren't you struggling to keep up?

194
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:50,359
But I didn't think it was this serious.

195
00:19:50,599 --> 00:19:53,240
Surgery? You've got to be kidding me.

196
00:19:54,799 --> 00:19:56,319
You should've said so when you came back.

197
00:19:57,440 --> 00:19:58,160
Just toughing it out.

198
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:01,680
Chief Liao, what was I supposed to say?

199
00:20:03,039 --> 00:20:04,319
We've been training for so many years.

200
00:20:05,599 --> 00:20:06,559
Who doesn't have a few injuries?

201
00:20:06,759 --> 00:20:07,759
Don't you have injuries too?

202
00:20:07,839 --> 00:20:08,920
Well, isn't it serious now?

203
00:20:09,039 --> 00:20:09,880
You could be paralyzed.

204
00:20:10,359 --> 00:20:11,839
We can't believe everything doctors say.

205
00:20:11,839 --> 00:20:12,359
Right.

206
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:13,640
He's an alarmist.

207
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:15,240
I told you, he's just an alarmist.

208
00:20:15,759 --> 00:20:17,359
Doctors really just try to scare people.

209
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:18,279
Just scaring us.

210
00:20:18,920 --> 00:20:21,079
You'll be in bed for a month at most.

211
00:20:21,319 --> 00:20:22,160
Then you'll be alive and kicking.

212
00:20:22,480 --> 00:20:23,559
And you'll come back to the team.

213
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:24,359
Exactly, exactly.

214
00:20:28,039 --> 00:20:29,400
Don't just stand around here. Go back now.

215
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:30,640
There's so much to do on the team.

216
00:20:30,759 --> 00:20:31,759
Let's go, let's go.

217
00:20:32,319 --> 00:20:32,720
All right.

218
00:20:34,319 --> 00:20:34,920
Get the surgery first.

219
00:20:35,119 --> 00:20:36,200
Okay, okay, the surgery.

220
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:37,759
Listen to the doctor carefully.

221
00:20:38,240 --> 00:20:39,119
All right, I got it.

222
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:50,839
Liu Lang.

223
00:20:52,319 --> 00:20:54,359
I haven't forgotten what I promised you.

224
00:20:54,759 --> 00:20:56,359
Good. You can't forget.

225
00:20:56,599 --> 00:20:57,240
I won't. I won't.

226
00:21:37,680 --> 00:21:38,240
Honey.

227
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:40,440
I've got some good news.

228
00:21:43,680 --> 00:21:45,400
I'm out of the Combat Skills Competition.

229
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:46,960
I'll be home soon.

230
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:51,000
Yeah, yeah. I'm heading back right now.

231
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:54,119
I'm done with the Special Police Unit.

232
00:21:54,279 --> 00:21:55,319
I'm done. I'm done. I'm done.

233
00:21:55,400 --> 00:21:55,839
Don't worry.

234
00:21:59,319 --> 00:22:00,839
Okay, okay. I'm hanging up now.

235
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:39,400
Chief Liao, a package for you.

236
00:22:43,279 --> 00:22:44,319
I didn't order anything.

237
00:22:44,640 --> 00:22:45,279
But it's for you.

238
00:22:45,279 --> 00:22:46,440
Doesn't it say the recipient is

239
00:22:46,680 --> 00:22:47,359
Tom Hardy?

240
00:25:40,359 --> 00:25:40,880
Right here. Right here.

241
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:08,799
Come on.

242
00:26:09,039 --> 00:26:09,440
What are you looking at?

243
00:26:09,960 --> 00:26:10,599
Where to?

244
00:26:11,279 --> 00:26:11,799
The courtyard.

245
00:26:12,680 --> 00:26:13,000
Let's go.

246
00:27:07,160 --> 00:27:08,200
In this competition,

247
00:27:08,960 --> 00:27:10,880
our only rival is Lvteng.

248
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:12,240
Still, we need to be careful.

249
00:27:12,599 --> 00:27:13,640
Don't let a dark horse sneak up on us.

250
00:27:29,559 --> 00:27:30,319
9.23 seconds.

251
00:27:31,680 --> 00:27:32,200
Clap!

252
00:27:54,319 --> 00:27:55,119
9.10 seconds.

253
00:29:02,519 --> 00:29:03,720
Team Obstacle Course

254
00:29:04,039 --> 00:29:04,920
The total score is ten points.

255
00:29:05,160 --> 00:29:05,920
One point for teamwork.

256
00:29:06,640 --> 00:29:07,680
Extra points are what matters.

257
00:29:09,240 --> 00:29:10,279
The baseline is three and a half minutes.

258
00:29:10,400 --> 00:29:11,640
One point for every five seconds faster.

259
00:29:12,039 --> 00:29:13,559
Even if we hit three twenty,

260
00:29:13,680 --> 00:29:15,079
we'd only tie at best.

261
00:29:15,720 --> 00:29:16,400
If we want to win,

262
00:29:17,079 --> 00:29:18,319
we have to break three fifteen.

263
00:29:20,720 --> 00:29:22,440
Then let's break three fifteen.

264
00:29:23,400 --> 00:29:24,079
That's too hard.

265
00:29:25,400 --> 00:29:25,839
Listen up, team,

266
00:29:27,599 --> 00:29:28,519
our goal

267
00:29:28,799 --> 00:29:30,599
isn't just about the numbers.

268
00:29:31,640 --> 00:29:32,599
Forget about Lvteng,

269
00:29:33,240 --> 00:29:33,960
and forget about the time.

270
00:29:34,319 --> 00:29:36,200
Just look ahead and focus on yourselves.

271
00:29:37,359 --> 00:29:39,400
Even a one-second improvement

272
00:29:40,039 --> 00:29:42,119
means beating your past selves.

273
00:29:42,880 --> 00:29:44,200
Come on, give it your all!

274
00:29:44,519 --> 00:29:45,200
Just do it!

275
00:29:47,640 --> 00:29:50,799
Do it! Do it! Do it!

276
00:29:59,599 --> 00:30:15,880
Let's go! Let's go! Let's go!

277
00:30:26,640 --> 00:30:32,559
Come on, come on, come on!

278
00:31:46,279 --> 00:31:47,440
Congratulations, Commissar Tan.

279
00:31:48,079 --> 00:31:49,640
The Special Police Unit did Red Leaf proud.

280
00:31:50,240 --> 00:31:51,240
I've already thought of a headline.

281
00:31:51,880 --> 00:31:54,880
"Red Leaf Special Police Deploy to Lvteng,

282
00:31:55,559 --> 00:31:56,880
The Road to Victory is a Breeze."

283
00:31:58,920 --> 00:31:59,920
That's a bit much, Chief Zhao.

284
00:32:00,359 --> 00:32:02,119
We didn't win easily this time.

285
00:32:03,599 --> 00:32:04,880
It's better to stick to the facts.

286
00:32:08,680 --> 00:32:09,000
Salute!

287
00:32:22,680 --> 00:32:23,160
Okay.

288
00:33:20,480 --> 00:33:21,920
About Liu Lang's reassignment...

289
00:33:22,559 --> 00:33:23,079
I've read it.

290
00:33:25,480 --> 00:33:27,440
You've worked in publicity for years.

291
00:33:28,079 --> 00:33:29,359
As a publicity officer,

292
00:33:30,160 --> 00:33:33,720
you must speak, observe, and write well.

293
00:33:35,440 --> 00:33:35,720
Yes.

294
00:33:37,319 --> 00:33:39,000
That's why Comrade Liu Lang is suitable.

295
00:33:40,960 --> 00:33:41,640
Most importantly,

296
00:33:41,640 --> 00:33:43,559
it's his true passion for being a cop.

297
00:33:44,519 --> 00:33:45,799
Such genuine feelings

298
00:33:46,240 --> 00:33:47,079
are incredibly rare.

299
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:48,640
What do you think?

300
00:33:50,119 --> 00:33:51,000
The right person

301
00:33:52,119 --> 00:33:53,160
doing the right job.

302
00:33:54,119 --> 00:33:54,440
It's good.

303
00:33:59,359 --> 00:34:01,920
Old Yu transferred from the Political Department to the Provincial Department.

304
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:02,720
Have you heard?

305
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:04,599
I have.

306
00:34:06,039 --> 00:34:07,480
The affairs of the Political Department

307
00:34:07,839 --> 00:34:09,639
need a suitable person to manage them.

308
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:13,719
Think about it.

309
00:34:20,360 --> 00:34:20,920
Chief Guo,

310
00:34:21,320 --> 00:34:23,280
I promised you I'd serve a full two years.

311
00:34:23,760 --> 00:34:25,039
I can't quit halfway through.

312
00:34:27,639 --> 00:34:28,679
This is a great opportunity.

313
00:34:31,559 --> 00:34:31,960
I understand.

314
00:34:35,719 --> 00:34:38,960
Your time in the Special Police Unit,

315
00:34:39,719 --> 00:34:40,920
you've changed quite a bit.

316
00:34:43,960 --> 00:34:47,079
Yes. After all, a daily 5K run,

317
00:34:47,880 --> 00:34:49,960
100 Weighted squats,

318
00:34:50,639 --> 00:34:52,320
and at least 300 sit-ups.

319
00:34:52,599 --> 00:34:53,960
Plus 120 on the bench press.

320
00:34:54,320 --> 00:34:55,639
It'd be hard not to change.

321
00:35:03,480 --> 00:35:03,960
Chief Guo,

322
00:35:04,679 --> 00:35:06,960
I heard our city stadium is moving.

323
00:35:08,039 --> 00:35:08,800
That plot of land

324
00:35:09,480 --> 00:35:10,119
is quite large.

325
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:14,559
The tides...

326
00:35:15,800 --> 00:35:16,679
You have to time them right.

327
00:35:19,039 --> 00:35:21,039
Then let's prepare to go beachcombing.

328
00:35:23,000 --> 00:35:24,440
In keeping with your habit,

329
00:35:25,760 --> 00:35:27,119
seeing this scenery,

330
00:35:29,239 --> 00:35:30,599
I suddenly feel like composing a poem too.

331
00:35:31,280 --> 00:35:31,599
Please do.

332
00:35:34,559 --> 00:35:35,639
Sitting and watching

333
00:35:37,159 --> 00:35:38,079
the rising tide

334
00:35:40,280 --> 00:35:41,239
between sky and sea,

335
00:35:42,679 --> 00:35:46,159
casting a line afar, finally at peace.

336
00:35:48,519 --> 00:35:49,760
The sea breeze...

337
00:35:52,880 --> 00:35:53,760
The sea breeze...

338
00:35:55,280 --> 00:35:55,880
At peace...

339
00:35:56,559 --> 00:35:57,599
Let me finish the last two lines.

340
00:35:58,199 --> 00:35:58,719
Go ahead, go ahead.

341
00:36:02,360 --> 00:36:03,559
The sea breeze brushes the face,

342
00:36:04,400 --> 00:36:05,440
the heart steadies on its own,

343
00:36:12,960 --> 00:36:14,760
asking not of storms or fleeting years.

344
00:36:20,719 --> 00:36:20,960
Excellent.

345
00:36:47,800 --> 00:36:48,280
Old Lu.

346
00:36:49,719 --> 00:36:51,320
The tomatoes are ripe.

347
00:36:53,719 --> 00:36:54,920
They're all nice and red.

348
00:36:55,960 --> 00:36:57,039
I brought some for you to taste.

349
00:37:06,440 --> 00:37:09,920
We won the Combat Skills Competition team title.

350
00:37:13,920 --> 00:37:15,599
You said the first-place podium is high.

351
00:37:18,039 --> 00:37:19,480
We all stood in a line.

352
00:37:20,920 --> 00:37:22,199
And I was the shortest.

353
00:37:30,840 --> 00:37:32,280
Things are going well in the team now.

354
00:37:34,519 --> 00:37:35,679
Everyone is working hard.

355
00:37:37,679 --> 00:37:40,280
We got new Civilian Recruitment members.

356
00:37:41,239 --> 00:37:42,360
They're all highly qualified.

357
00:37:49,920 --> 00:37:51,039
Some people come.

358
00:37:51,880 --> 00:37:52,960
And some people go.

359
00:37:59,360 --> 00:37:59,800
Liu Lang.

360
00:38:00,599 --> 00:38:02,440
Old Liu really couldn't hold on this time.

361
00:38:03,840 --> 00:38:05,000
His back injury flared up.

362
00:38:06,800 --> 00:38:07,920
He was almost paralyzed.

363
00:38:09,400 --> 00:38:10,920
Luckily, the surgery went well.

364
00:38:12,480 --> 00:38:14,039
He'll be fine after a two-month recovery.

365
00:38:16,039 --> 00:38:17,280
He went to the Publicity Department.

366
00:38:21,360 --> 00:38:22,000
It suits him.

367
00:38:24,199 --> 00:38:24,719
Lü Xiao.

368
00:38:27,119 --> 00:38:27,960
Went to Criminal Investigation.

369
00:38:31,960 --> 00:38:34,599
He wanted Criminal Investigation since day one.

370
00:38:36,320 --> 00:38:37,559
I guess his dream finally came true.

371
00:38:39,079 --> 00:38:41,559
And our new Political Commissar, Tan.

372
00:38:42,559 --> 00:38:43,880
Though he's not exactly new.

373
00:38:47,199 --> 00:38:48,000
He's doing well too.

374
00:38:49,880 --> 00:38:51,760
He just nags even more than you did.

375
00:38:58,280 --> 00:38:59,800
Ma'am and the kid...

376
00:39:01,280 --> 00:39:02,199
...are doing fine too.

377
00:39:04,639 --> 00:39:05,559
Everyone is doing fine.

378
00:39:09,079 --> 00:39:09,719
I'm doing fine too.

379
00:39:18,079 --> 00:39:19,079
I just miss you.

380
00:39:35,400 --> 00:39:36,559
With Jianan in her current condition,

381
00:39:36,559 --> 00:39:37,559
recovery is going to be really difficult.

382
00:39:38,320 --> 00:39:39,239
Are you just going to keep helping her?

383
00:39:40,280 --> 00:39:41,000
Forever?

384
00:39:43,639 --> 00:39:44,519
Isn't what you're doing right now

385
00:39:44,519 --> 00:39:45,960
going beyond just being a friend?

386
00:39:51,960 --> 00:39:54,599
Remember my past before joining the team?

387
00:39:55,280 --> 00:39:55,840
Yeah, I do.

388
00:39:55,840 --> 00:39:57,159
Weren't you pretty lost back then?

389
00:39:58,239 --> 00:39:59,360
Commissar Lu lit the way for you.

390
00:40:01,519 --> 00:40:03,719
Yeah, Commissar Lu lit the way for me.

391
00:40:04,960 --> 00:40:05,960
He was the very first person

392
00:40:05,960 --> 00:40:07,719
to encourage and believe in me.

393
00:40:09,719 --> 00:40:10,320
He said

394
00:40:11,639 --> 00:40:13,400
I didn't just have a talent for shooting,

395
00:40:15,320 --> 00:40:17,760
but I could also do something more.

396
00:40:21,000 --> 00:40:22,400
I remember Jianan once wrote

397
00:40:22,400 --> 00:40:23,360
a certain line in her diary.

398
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:28,559
She said I was her ray of light.

399
00:40:30,639 --> 00:40:32,039
So I was thinking,

400
00:40:34,599 --> 00:40:36,400
maybe I could do something for her.

401
00:40:37,360 --> 00:40:39,719
Maybe I could tell her

402
00:40:40,599 --> 00:40:42,000
that she still has a long life ahead.

403
00:40:44,960 --> 00:40:46,360
Commissar Lu was my ray of light too.

404
00:40:49,199 --> 00:40:50,119
And you're my ray of light.

405
00:40:52,599 --> 00:40:53,119
What did you say?

406
00:40:56,320 --> 00:40:57,960
You're acting more like Commissar Lu.

407
00:41:30,159 --> 00:41:31,440
Welcome, welcome, welcome!

408
00:41:31,480 --> 00:41:31,880
Chief Zhao!

409
00:41:31,880 --> 00:41:32,519
Welcome, welcome.

410
00:41:34,880 --> 00:41:35,840
Welcome to our big family...

411
00:41:35,840 --> 00:41:37,119
...of the Publicity Department!

412
00:41:37,119 --> 00:41:38,320
Thank you. Thank you.

413
00:41:52,159 --> 00:41:52,960
What do you mean he got away?

414
00:41:53,599 --> 00:41:54,559
I don't want to hear excuses.

415
00:41:54,559 --> 00:41:55,639
I only want results.

416
00:41:56,559 --> 00:41:58,159
Don't you know what your job is?

417
00:41:58,480 --> 00:41:59,960
You're police officers, understand?

418
00:42:00,679 --> 00:42:01,239
I'm sorry.

419
00:42:01,719 --> 00:42:02,159
Captain Zhang.

420
00:42:02,519 --> 00:42:03,280
Save it.

421
00:42:04,360 --> 00:42:05,119
I'm in the back alley.

422
00:42:05,320 --> 00:42:06,239
Hurry up and get over here.

423
00:42:16,679 --> 00:42:17,320
Don't move. Don't move.

424
00:42:17,320 --> 00:42:17,920
Okay, okay, okay.

425
00:42:18,559 --> 00:42:19,039
Okay. Okay.

426
00:42:20,199 --> 00:42:20,559
Okay. Okay.

427
00:42:20,559 --> 00:42:21,639
Now, don't move. Don't move.
